    "body": "Somehow github's \"commit suggestion\" UI wouldn't commit the suggestion... but I've incorporated it into the edit that I'll push shortly.  I've edited the wording a bit but I don't think I've changed the substance.\r\n\r\nOne note is that I'm not a fan of \"programatically\" here (though I've left it for now) because that feels like it's referring to code in a programming language rather than tree structure of markup, but I'm not sure what alternative might be better.  Maybe \"structurally\" or \"logically\"?",
